  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Meeting critical needs of migrants in situations of vulnerability, internally displaced persons and host communities in YemenMeeting critical needs of migrants in situations of vulnerability, internally displaced persons and host communities in Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Severe humanitarian needs remain across Yemen, especially for families living in protracted displacement, conflict-affected host community members and vulnerable migrants. In 2024, an escalation in conflict, disease outbreak and severe weather incidents greatly impacted numerous already vulnerable households in Yemen, leading to more than 19 million individuals in need of assistance in 2025. The proposed multisectoral intervention ensures the most vulnerable internally displaced persons (IDPs), host community members, and migrants throughout the country have access to core services to meet urgent needs and contribute to safe and dignified living conditions. The intervention not only addresses immediate needs but also contributes to reducing dependency on humanitarian assistance by promoting local ownership, integrating progressive exit strategies from emergency solutions, and building productive capacities of vulnerable households, in addition, to supporting displaced populations outside of sites and the surrounding host community.</narrative>
  </description>
